        "id": "p20-q51-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $c=-\\ln|b|$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p20-q51-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "c=-\\ln|b|",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", with ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "b>0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p20-q51-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Equating the reflected rule with ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " gives ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x^2=\\dfrac{b^2-e^{-2c}}{a^2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". Exactly one intersection requires ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x^2=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Reflecting in both axes gives $g(x)=-f(-x)=-\\ln(b-ax)-c$. At an intersection,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\ln(ax+b)+c&=-\\ln(b-ax)-c\\\\\\ln(ax+b)+\\ln(b-ax)&=-2c\\\\\\ln(b^2-a^2x^2)&=-2c\\\\b^2-a^2x^2&=e^{-2c}\\\\x^2&=\\dfrac{b^2-e^{-2c}}{a^2}.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth logarithmic arguments must be positive, so $b>0$ and $|ax|<b$. A positive value of $x^2$ gives two admissible intersections, while a negative value gives none. Exactly one intersection therefore requires $x^2=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}b^2&=e^{-2c}\\\\c&=-\\tfrac12\\ln(b^2)\\\\c&=-\\ln|b|.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 102
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q51-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the coordinates of the intersection.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(0,0)$.",
          "worked": "From part a, the unique intersection has $x=0$ and $b>0$. Substitute $c=-\\ln b$ into $f(0)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\ln b+c\\\\y&=\\ln b-\\ln b\\\\y&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe point of intersection is $(0,0)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
